 rulings:{
  'SE-A':ruling('APPROVED','No prescription changes before a return.',SEAFACT),
  'SE-B':ruling('APPROVED_WITH_CONDITIONS (NF-R7ASE-1 routed as R41)','A return starts from what the athlete executed, value by value; after weeks never reported the run starts from its last evidence-anchored value, which can sit below what reported weeks executed (conservative).',SEBFACT+' '+E5FACT),
  'SE-C':ruling('APPROVED','A known load lifted is the load, by the review’s own adoption rule (D44); effort-guided rows adopt nothing (my R7AB S-B).',SEBFACT),
  'SE-D':ruling('APPROVED_WITH_CONDITIONS (the load and its repetition target; not a stored tick only the projection counted: NF-R7ASE-3 routed as R42)','A projected dose lifted exactly is history for its load and repetition target; with repetitions unlogged the load is the fact, the repetitions stay the target, no step (Founder §13 applied to what is missing). The stored load tick it carries can count an exposure the projection assumed; that part is not approved as history, though its sporting reach equals the unchanged planner’s no-break progression.',SEBFACT+' '+TICKFACT),
  'SE-E':ruling('APPROVED (R40 applied; NF-R7AB-1 resolved)','Per sport: a sport executed exactly as projected keeps its completed sessions; each sport equals or trails its reviewed control.',SEEFACT),
  'SE-F':ruling('APPROVED','A review’s carried values are rebuilt by its own rule on history; Sunday handlers applying the review’s rule review that sport (E6).',SEFFACT),
  'SE-G':ruling('APPROVED','Last performed is the execution date in history: the correct input for a days-since-exposure threshold; the planner’s own threshold stays on the planning view (E1).','Test "§8 last performed date" passes in my suite run; every grid byte-identical.'),
  'SE-H':ruling('APPROVED as declared boundaries (NF-R7ASE-2 recorded for E2; NF-R7ASE-1 for E5)','E1-E6 are planning-view or conservative-history boundaries; none lets a projected value reach a return.',E2FACT+' '+E5FACT)},
 blockers:{status:'D53 CLOSED (holds); D56 holds; D57 holds; D58 holds; D59 CLOSED (holds); QE-R7AF-01 closed in my scope',
  D53:'CLOSED, holds: S-F checks 0 on 22 paths (no unexecuted return step, load or whole count reaches a ceiling or a resumed dose); the projected-load class is gone from my P40 cells (loads never lifted 0, against 6 on the boundary freeze); F-A byte-identical. The tick exception NF-R7ASE-3 is outside D53’s step, load and count scope and does not exceed the no-break planner.',
  D56:'Holds: 0 cap rises or ends after a non-whole week; caps grids byte-identical.',D57:'Holds: restoration grid B 0, C 0; caps 0 unexplained; byte-identical.',D58:'Holds: short grid 0 defects; D58 readings byte-identical; one easy slot per break (H17’s eased slot follows D58 on the historical quality state).',
  D59:'CLOSED, holds: first-week grid E = O = B = 0 for every class; extended grid and ceiling equality 0; byte-identical.','QE-R7AF-01':'Closed in my scope: my R7-A final probes byte-identical.'},
 newFindings:[
  {id:'NF-R7ASE-1',severity:'NON_BLOCKING',items:['SE-B','SE-H E5'],finding:'After weeks never reported, history promotes the run value only by a review’s rule on a historical base or by completed sessions on a historical base, so a return can start the run below what reported weeks executed. R6-H17 (5-day break): long run 85 after an executed 95, quality ladder at step 0, strides uncounted. R6-H26 (17-day break): week 5 executed in full (long run 100) but reviewed KEEP, which records no evidence start, so the run value is the intake’s (regain target 80) and the second return week prescribes a 50-minute long run (65 on the boundary freeze; the holdout assessment prefers about 70-80% of the last long run). Strength reported without loads keeps its last known loads (Founder §13).',whyNotBlocking:'It raises no dose and breaks no declared rule: every output is the approved recipe from an executed or reported state, at or below the boundary freeze. It needs weeks left unreported before the break, which the Founder rules not history (§1, §11). The cost is progression, not safety (R6-S52).',recommendation:'R41'},
  {id:'NF-R7ASE-2',severity:'NON_BLOCKING (unchanged, not a regression)',items:['SE-H E2'],finding:'A run value read through an unreviewed week keeps that week’s evidence start and is not re-gated, so a long run missed in that week does not hold the target as a review would (P40b cells 6-8: U long 70 against R 65). The value was earned on executed work by an earlier review, not made by a projection; every other run counter now trails the control.',whyNotBlocking:'Unchanged since R7A-BOUNDARY-FINAL-FREEZE, which I accepted; one long-run step in a regain target; re-gating would break the week-boundary invariance (R7-A final P5).',recommendation:'Record only, for the next run-state mission.'},
  {id:'NF-R7ASE-3',severity:'NON_BLOCKING for this sporting gate; a state-evidence question for the Chief and the engineering judge (Founder §27, §28)',items:['SE-D'],finding:'The projected dose a lift promotes (contract §5) carries the stored start’s load tick, and that tick can count an exposure the projection assumed but the athlete did not execute. Back squat: week 2’s 82.5 kg row lifted at 80 kg and never reviewed (week 3 stored 82.5 kg tick 1); week 3 lifted 82.5 kg with its target missed; history 82.5 kg tick 1 (the unreviewed cell and its reviewed control alike; boundary freeze tick 0). After a 2-day return the load steps to 85 kg after one more successful exposure instead of two.',whyNotBlocking:'Sporting reach: one smallest increment (about 3%) one successful, RIR-gated exposure earlier, never above a lifted load’s ceiling in a moderate return, and identical to the unchanged planner’s own progression for the same history with no break (82.5 then 85 kg, reviewed weekly or not). The approved progression as the runtime applies it is therefore not exceeded. Whether a projection-made tick in history is a material state-evidence manifestation is the engineering judge’s call under Founder §27; I report it, I do not certify the tick atom.',recommendation:'R42'}],
 nonBlockingRecommendations:[
  {id:'R41',owner:'Runtime author with Product/UX and Data; a Founder decision if it is judged a state-model change',text:'(a) When a return follows weeks never reported, ask the athlete to confirm what those weeks contained; a confirmed factual report or correction is evidence (I6). (b) Make a KEEP weekly review of a complete week record its evidence for history as a MODIFY review does, so a fully executed, reviewed week is not read as unreviewed. (c) Consider value-scoped promotion of the run from completed executions in a reviewed week (for example, an executed long run as a floor of the run value’s regain target, bounded by the review’s own one-step rule), as a later state-model refinement; it changes a return’s dose, so it needs an SSCTR review before it binds. Until then keep the conservative reading.'},
  {id:'R42',owner:'Chief with the engineering judge (state evidence); runtime author in a later mission, never as a correction of this freeze',text:'When a lift promotes a projected dose (contract §5), take its load tick from history, not from the stored start: tick 0 at a load the history had not reached, or the historical tick when the historical value already held that load; then the executed exposure counts only through a review’s rule, as for every fact. Reword contract §5 accordingly (“its load ticks” would then read “the ticks the athlete executed at that load”). It lowers no load and changes no ceiling; it can only delay a load step by one successful exposure.'}],
 priorFindings:{'NF-R7AB-1 (R40)':'RESOLVED by SE-E (SD held 60/60/60/65; SB and the systemic case continue the executed run step).','NF-R7AF-1 (R38), NF-R7AF-2 (R39)':'Retained; F-D and F-F byte-identical.','R35, R36':'Retained for the next policy revision.','IS-7 cost bound':'Restated: at most the progress executed since the return in force, per sport.'},
